My major argument is actually that pudding farming creates an infinite
supply of items, experience, HP, AC (sacrifice, pray for golden glow,
sacrifice until timeout goes away, etc), score... etc.

This infinite supply of items, etc. can then be used to bypass most of
the rest of the game as necessary, creating a one-dimensional circumstance.

The next argument beyond that is that if you're on public servers, this
renders score not only meaningless (though it was meaningless for other
reasons), but it also renders any changes you might make to the scoring
system equally meaningless; so if I want to fix the scoring system, I
need to fix all the infinite-X abuses.  Pudding farming is the easiest
and most scriptable.  Rider farming is also scriptable, but as mentioned
in other threads, less of an immediate concern under the major argument
because, well, by the time you can Rider farm you've already completed
the game.

Pudding farmers who grow careless and die disrupt people who find their
bones; this is a public-server-only (and Hearse) problem, but it is
still a problem.

Oh, and one more -- it crashes the game eventually.  When ctaboir was
making an effort to tie Zadir's MAXINT-1 game, I think he had to have it
recovered _several_ times by paxed; this is really bad.

